{"annotationScore": 4.0, "comments": [{"commentType": "FUNCTION", "texts": [{"value": "Core component of nucleosome. Nucleosomes wrap and compact DNA into chromatin, limiting DNA accessibility to the cellular machineries which require DNA as a template. Histones thereby play a central role in transcription regulation, DNA repair, DNA replication and chromosomal stability. DNA accessibility is regulated via a complex set of post-translational modifications of histones, also called histone code, and nucleosome remodeling"}]}, {"commentType": "SUBUNIT", "texts": [{"value": "The nucleosome is a histone octamer containing two molecules each of H2A, H2B, H3 and H4 assembled in one H3-H4 heterotetramer and two H2A-H2B heterodimers. The octamer wraps approximately 147 bp of DNA"}]}, {"commentType": "SUBCELLULAR LOCATION", "subcellularLocations": [{"location": {"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250"}], "id": "SL-0191", "value": "Nucleus"}}, {"location": {"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250"}], "id": "SL-0468", "value": "Chromosome"}}]}, {"commentType": "ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS", "events": ["Alternative splicing"], "isoforms": [{"isoformIds": ["Q9BTM1-1"], "isoformSequenceStatus": "Displayed", "name": {"value": "1"}}, {"isoformIds": ["Q9BTM1-2"], "isoformSequenceStatus": "Described", "name": {"value": "2"}, "sequenceIds": ["VSP_034750"]}]}, {"commentType": "PTM", "texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250"}], "value": "Monoubiquitination of Lys-120 (H2AXK119ub) gives a specific tag for epigenetic transcriptional repression. Following DNA double-strand breaks (DSBs), it is ubiquitinated through 'Lys-63' linkage of ubiquitin moieties (By similarity)"}]}, {"commentType": "PTM", "texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250"}], "value": "Phosphorylation on Ser-2 (H2AS1ph) is enhanced during mitosis. Phosphorylation on Ser-2 by RPS6KA5/MSK1 directly represses transcription. Acetylation of H3 inhibits Ser-2 phosphorylation by RPS6KA5/MSK1. Phosphorylation at Thr-121 (H2AT120ph) by DCAF1 is present in the regulatory region of many tumor suppresor genes and down-regulates their transcription (By similarity)"}]}, {"commentType": "PTM", "texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250"}], "value": "Glutamine methylation at Gln-105 (H2AQ104me) by FBL is specifically dedicated to polymerase I. It is present at 35S ribosomal DNA locus and impairs binding of the FACT complex (By similarity)"}]}, {"commentType": "SIMILARITY", "texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000305"}], "value": "Belongs to the histone H2A family"}]}], "entryAudit": {"entryVersion": 178, "firstPublicDate": "2008-07-22", "lastAnnotationUpdateDate": "2026-11-04", "lastSequenceUpdateDate": "2001-06-01", "sequenceVersion": 1}, "entryType": "UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)", "extraAttributes": {"countByCommentType": {"ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS": 2, "FUNCTION": 1, "PTM": 3, "SIMILARITY": 1, "SUBCELLULAR LOCATION": 1, "SUBUNIT": 1}, "countByFeatureType": {"Alternative sequence": 1, "Beta strand": 3, "Chain": 1, "Compositional bias": 1, "Helix": 6, "Initiator methionine": 1, "Modified residue": 5, "Region": 1, "Turn": 1}, "uniParcId": "UPI000006D12E"}, "features": [{"description": "Removed", "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000305"}], "location": {"end": {"modifier": "EXACT", "value": 1}, "start": {"modifier": "EXACT", "value": 1}}, "type": "Initiator methionine"}, {"description": "Histone H2A.J", "featureId": "PRO_0000344247", "location": {"end": {"modifier": "EXACT", "value": 129}, "start": {"modifier": "EXACT", "value": 2}}, "type": "Chain"}, {"description": "Disordered", "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000256", "id": "MobiDB-lite", "source": "SAM"}], "location": {"end": {"modifier": "EXACT", "value": 22}, "start": {"modifier": "EXACT", "value": 1}}, "type": "Region"}, {"description": "Basic residues", "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000256", "id": "MobiDB-lite", "source": "SAM"}], "location": {"end": {"modifier": "EXACT", "value